msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:8
msgid "While writing code"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:10
msgid ""
"Verify that you understand the preconditions of any `unsafe` functions/traits"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:11
msgid "Check that the preconditions are satisfied"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:12
msgid "Document your reasoning in safety comments"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:14
msgid "Enhanced code review"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:16
msgid "Self-review → peer reviewer → unsafe Rust expert (when needed)"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:17
msgid "Escalate to a person who is comfortable with your code and reasoning"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:22
msgid ""
"“The unsafe keyword places more responsibility on the programmer; therefore "
"it requires a stronger development workflow."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:25
msgid ""
"“This class assumes a specific software development workflow where code "
"review is mandatory, and where the author and primary reviewer have access "
"to an unsafe Rust expert.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:29
msgid ""
"“The author and primary reviewer will verify simple unsafe Rust code "
"themselves, and punt to an unsafe expert when necessary.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/impact-on-workflow.md:32
msgid ""
"“There are only a few unsafe Rust experts, and they are very busy, so we "
"need to optimally use their time.”"
msgstr ""
